<section class="w-full px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <header class="mb-12 max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-5xl">About 16-0 Play</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--color-body)]">16-0 Play is an independent cricket game. Build a squad, simulate a season and compare runs on the leaderboard.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-base leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">
      <p>Play solo or with others. We are not affiliated with the IPL or any cricket board.</p>
      <section class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="about-how-it-works">
        <h2 id="about-how-it-works" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">How the game works</h2>
        <p>16-0 Play is a browser-based cricket strategy game built around squad selection and simulated seasons. Players in the game's database have a role, team, season record, and an internal overall rating. In the standard mode, you select eleven players. The engine uses role-weighted batting and bowling values, then adjusts team strength for roster composition, selected chemistry and rivalry pairs, overseas count, and other thresholds. Match outcomes include random variation, so the displayed strength is an input to the simulation rather than a promise about the next result.</p>
        <p>The game has Classic, Franchise, Gamble, and Multiplayer modes. Classic is the direct XI-building flow; Franchise offers a larger roster and match preparation; Gamble generates a side from a random team philosophy; Multiplayer connects a room for a timed auction. Controls and roster constraints differ by mode. The current league fixture generator creates fourteen regular-season matches per team across two groups, followed by a playoff bracket for the top four. The “16-0” name is the challenge goal, not a description of sixteen league fixtures.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="about-data-sources">
        <h2 id="about-data-sources" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Game data and sources</h2>
        <p>The ratings and role labels are part of the site's game database. They are internal game values, not official ratings or a ranking of real-world ability. Player profile career totals are computed from Cricsheet's public IPL ball-by-ball records when a player can be matched to a stable Cricsheet identifier with high confidence. The profile labels the source and links to the <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="https://cricsheet.org/register/">Cricsheet Register</a>. If a profile does not show career statistics, the name matching was left unresolved rather than guessed.</p>
        <p>Cricsheet's Register is published under the Open Data Commons Attribution license (ODC-BY 1.0). The player-stat pipeline keeps that Register attribution separate from the ball-by-ball archive; the official pages reviewed do not specify a license for the match archive. Statistics describe the source data and the game's stated counting rules, and should not be mistaken for official competition records.</p>
        <p>The website is maintained as an independent project. It does not publish a named author or development team on this page. 16-0 Play is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the IPL, BCCI, or any franchise.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="about-more-information">
        <h2 id="about-more-information" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Learn more</h2>
        <p>For practical help, read the <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="/guides/">strategy guides</a>, browse the <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="/players">player database</a>, or review the <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="/rating-system">rating system</a>. The <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> explains browser storage, analytics, contact messages, and multiplayer connections.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="about-how-to-read-data">
        <h2 id="about-how-to-read-data" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">How to read the numbers</h2>
        <p>The site's player pages combine game-database information with an optional source-backed career record. The profile rating and role are used by the game. Cricsheet career totals, when available, are derived from ball-by-ball files and a player register using stable identifiers. The two datasets use different purposes and should not be combined as though the career total is the formula for the rating.</p>
        <p>The stat builder runs before page generation and saves a static JSON file in the project. Player pages do not fetch match data from Cricsheet in the visitor's browser. A matching script accepts only unique normalized names or register aliases; ambiguous or unmatched identities are listed for review. This conservative choice means some profiles have no table even when the source archive may contain a similarly named player.</p>
        <p>Game rules can change as the project evolves. The guides describe the code and data inspected for the current site build, and the navigation links take you to the related details. They are not claims about official competition rules. A match simulation may simplify real cricket events, and a generated score should not be read as a prediction or historical record.</p>
      </section>
      <p>Questions or feedback? <a class="font-medium text-[var(--color-link)] underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-link-deep)]" href="/contact">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
